From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:03:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] settings: Safety & Alerts has the nozzle-hit guard

Kiln's shipped plugin nozzle-guard (off by default) pauses a print when
the bed weighing board feels the nozzle hit the print or the bed; with
it on, Klipper has the ad5x_nozzle_guard object (enabled, sensitivity,
threshold, ...) and NOZZLE_GUARD ENABLE=0|1 and SENSITIVITY=low|medium|
high change it, saved, no restart.

Settings > Safety & Alerts gets two rows, only on a Kiln OS printer (one
with ad5x_weight): "Nozzle-hit guard", a switch ("Pause the print if the
nozzle hits the print or the bed"), and "Sensitivity" (Low, Medium,
High; 600, 300, 150 g) while the guard is on. A "custom" limit
(NOZZLE_GUARD THRESHOLD=) shows as the nearest choice.

The switch, without the object (the plugin off): on asks first with the
confirmation Settings > Plugins shows for it (ad5x_toggle_confirm(),
patch 0005: "Turn on the nozzle-hit guard?", "Klipper restarts to apply
this. Continue?") and sends ENABLE_PLUGIN NAME=nozzle-guard, handled as
that page sends it (the restart drops the reply; the expected-restart
notice). The switch stays on and locked until the discovery after the
restart, which sees the object; when Klipper doesn't go down within 15 s
of the answer (already enabled), the switch shows Klipper's state again.
Klipper refuses ENABLE_PLUGIN during a print, so then the switch is
locked with the line "Can be turned on when no print is running (Klipper
restarts)". With the object: NOZZLE_GUARD ENABLE=1|0, also during a
print. A refusal shows Klipper's message and puts the switch back.

Ad5xNozzleGuardModel (ui_settings_ad5x_nozzle_guard.cpp) follows the
object as Ad5xLogModel (patch 0049) does: a tail discovery step
(ad5x_nozzle_guard_watch) attaches it on every discovery, the
subscription takes enabled, sensitivity and threshold only (print_peak
changes during a print), the Safety overlay registers its subjects and
asks Klipper when it opens.

On a hit the module writes "!! Nozzle hit detected: ..." and pauses: the
pause overlay already shows that line as the reason (print_stop_reason),
and the filament runout explanation replaces it only when a loaded
lane's sensor reads empty. A test pins the line as the pause reason.

The new strings are in en.yml and, as in patch 0097, in de, es, fr, it,
ja, ko, pt, ru, tr and zh, with each file's own words for nozzle, print,
bed, sensitivity and "Klipper restarts". "the nozzle-hit guard" goes
into the "Turn on {}?" title, so each language has the form that fits
there (Russian in the accusative, German and Turkish without an article).
Japanese and Chinese name it with characters the baked CJK fonts have
("contact" and "impact": the usual words for collision are not
baked). The question's "Klipper restarts to apply this. Continue?" was
in en.yml and ru.yml only; the other nine get it here (patches 0005,
0008 and 0009 ask it too).
